-- =============================================================================
-- Metadata Sync — v1.3.x release
-- =============================================================================
--
-- Generated by `mj sync push --dir metadata --ci` against COMM_SQL_SYNC: a clean
-- SQL Server database built from migrations ONLY — MJ core (next), bizapps-common
-- (next), bizapps-tasks, then every bizapps-committees migration through
-- V202607072300 — with no prior sync of this app's metadata, per the release-time
-- metadata sync ritual (see bizapps-common's V202608140800 and V202609020500, and
-- bizapps-tasks' V202608270002, for the documented corrections). The push reported
-- 0 errors: 27 created, 82 updated, 109 records. This file is the emitted
-- metadata/sql_logging/MetadataSync_Push_2026-09-18T16-54-59-007Z.sql with its
-- schema references corrected (see SUBSTITUTIONS below).
--
-- WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. v1.0.0–v1.1.1 shipped a SQL Server sync,
-- V202607080009__v1.0.x__Metadata_Sync.sql. It was deleted on 2026-09-06 (4d15aa4,
-- PR #38) because its spCreateFileStorageProvider call failed against an MJ core
-- regression, so v1.2.0 shipped with NO SQL Server metadata sync at all
-- (migrations-pg/ still carries V202607080009). `mj-app.json`'s
-- `metadata.directory` is a dev-time pointer the install engine never reads, so
-- a SQL Server install got the schema and code with none of the seed metadata
-- below. This is deliberately the LAST migration of the release so it captures
-- metadata state after all schema work.
--
-- THIS REPLACES V202607080009 RATHER THAN BUILDING ON IT. It is a full capture
-- against a database that never ran that file, and it re-creates the same 27
-- record IDs (Types, Roles, Artifact Types, Credential Type, File Storage
-- Provider, AI Prompt, AI Agent, AI Agent Prompt). Do not restore V202607080009
-- alongside this file.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT SEED CREATES. This file originally assumed no SQL Server install of
-- v1.0.0–v1.1.1 existed outside development, and stated that a database which DID
-- apply V202607080009 would hit primary-key violations here and had to be rebuilt.
-- That assumption was wrong: such installs exist, and on one of them this migration
-- aborted at batch 1/112 with
--
--     Violation of PRIMARY KEY constraint 'PK__Credenti__3214EC27D685D4A7'.
--     Cannot insert duplicate key in object '__mj.CredentialType'.
--     The duplicate key value is (daa02013-510d-41f4-bfaa-9250c7bc7d37).
--
-- taking the whole upgrade with it. Rebuilding a live schema is not an available
-- remedy, so every one of the 29 spCreate* calls below is now guarded by an
-- IF NOT EXISTS on its own primary key. On a fresh database all 29 create as
-- before; on a database that already ran V202607080009 the 27 shared IDs are
-- skipped and only the genuinely new Template and TemplateContent are created.
-- The 82 spUpdate* calls need no guard — spUpdate* already no-ops on an absent ID.
--
-- The guards do NOT converge an existing row's CONTENT to this capture. They make
-- the migration survivable, not authoritative; a host that wants the newer field
-- values for those 27 records should re-run `mj sync push` against metadata/.
--
-- WHAT THIS CARRIES — the delta between metadata/ (source of truth) and a
-- database built purely from migrations:
--   * Committees: Types — 5 created
--   * Committees: Roles — 8 created
--   * Committees: Artifact Types — 9 created
--   * MJ: Credential Types — 1 created
--   * MJ: File Storage Providers — 1 created
--   * MJ: Templates / Template Contents / AI Prompts — 1 each (Committee Importer
--     system prompt)
--   * MJ: AI Agents / AI Agent Prompts — 1 each (Committee Importer agent)
--   * MJ: Entities — 11 updates (metadata/entities/: form layout, search API
--     curation, disabled zombie entities)
--   * MJ: Entity Fields — 49 updates (metadata/entity-fields/ and field pins
--     from metadata/entities/)
--   * MJ: Entity Relationships — 22 updates (form-chrome placement from
--     metadata/entity-relationships/)
--
-- SUBSTITUTIONS APPLIED TO THE GENERATOR'S OUTPUT
--
--   `[${flyway:defaultSchema}]`   ->  `[${mjSchema}]`               89 occurrences
--   `[__mj_BizAppsCommittees]`    ->  `[${flyway:defaultSchema}]`   22 occurrences
--
-- The first is a correction, not a rename. `sqlLogging.formatAsMigration` emits
-- core stored-procedure calls as `[${flyway:defaultSchema}]`, which is right only
-- when the Flyway default schema IS the MJ core schema. Here
-- `mj migrate --schema __mj_BizAppsCommittees` binds it to THIS app's schema.
-- Verified against the build database: spUpdateEntity, spUpdateEntityField,
-- spUpdateEntityRelationship, spCreateCredentialType, spCreateFileStorageProvider,
-- spCreateTemplate, spCreateTemplateContent, spCreateAIPrompt, spCreateAIAgent and
-- spCreateAIAgentPrompt exist in `__mj` only. This app's own procs — spCreateType,
-- spCreateRole, spCreateArtifactType — were left literal by the generator and now
-- carry `${flyway:defaultSchema}`. Note spCreateRole and spCreateArtifactType ALSO
-- exist in `__mj` (core Roles / Artifact Types), so the direction matters: these
-- 17 calls save `Committees: Roles` / `Committees: Artifact Types` and must hit
-- the app schema.
--
-- MJ CORE FLOOR: 6.1.0-edge.6. These are full-row procedure calls, so they carry
-- the core proc signatures of the database they were captured on. Two of them
-- need MJ migrations that first ship in v6.1.0-edge.6:
--   * spUpdateEntity @SubtypeSelector            (V202609081111 Entity_SubtypeSelector)
--   * spCreateFileStorageProvider @SupportsSearch / @RequiresOAuth
--                                                (V202609061800 Restore_FileStorageProvider_SP...)
-- On 6.1.0-edge.5 both calls fail ("not a parameter" / "too many arguments"), so
-- mj-app.json's mjVersionRange moved to >=6.1.0-edge.6 in the same change. No core
-- schema migration newer than edge.6 was present on the capture database.
--
-- INSTALL-SAFETY CHECKS (spUpdate* silently no-ops on an absent ID):
--   * All 82 Entity / Entity Field / Entity Relationship IDs updated here appear
--     literally in this repo's shipped migrations — none is install-generated.
--   * Every foreign-key GUID referenced but not created here resolves to a
--     shipped MJ core, bizapps-common, bizapps-tasks or bizapps-committees
--     migration. No user- or environment-specific IDs.
-- =============================================================================

